{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1483797-dark-kingdom-of-ice","id":1483797,"title":"Dark Kingdom of... Ice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-12T09:52:08-07:00","id":1483797,"title":"Dark Kingdom of... Ice?","content":"Okay<br /> So I can't really find the book or basically any reference to it, but I have foggy memories about reading about the Dark Kingdom of Ice (and made notes for my chronicle) for the dead of the North (mostly nordic people)<br /> It was... let's say not in this decade...<br /> But now, while working on a new chronicle I stumbled in to my own notes and wondered... where was it mentioned?<br /> Maybe some one can help me, to find the book it was published (I suspect it was a first edition thing) or my mind jus playing tricks with me again and this Dark Kingdom never officialy existed?<br /> About my notes:<br /> <br /> The Dark Kingdom of Ice is Niflheim, from whence the Queen of the Dead rules from her seat in her capitol city of Hel. The city of Hel lies amidst an icy mountain chain, and overlooks a deep abyss that supposedly drops straight into the Abyss. Within the naturally occurring ice it is said that many wonders may be found, but also many terrors. So, too, do they claim that a bridge exists in the mountains that leads to the land of the fey.<br /> <br /> Not much, I know...<br /> Anyhow, I hope for someone it rings a bell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T10:14:29-07:00","id":1483798,"title":"","content":"I don't remember one, although I've long considered it a bit of head canon that there was a Dark Kingdom of Ash (as in the tree/wood) in Germania, Scandinavia, and elsewhere that Stygia conquered at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T10:21:02-07:00","id":1483799,"title":"","content":"Yeah; it's a pretty cool bit of head-canon; but sadly, I think that's all it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T05:59:00-07:00","id":1483859,"title":"","content":"I think Dark Ages Mage might have something, I believe that book touched on the Old Norse afterlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T06:59:35-07:00","id":1483863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1483797-dark-kingdom-of-ice?p=1483859#post1483859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Dark Ages Mage might have something, I believe that book touched on the Old Norse afterlife.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 180 of Dark Ages Mage for specifics on Niflheim. Pages 174-181 for the whole section on the Dark Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:52:21-07:00","id":1483914,"title":"","content":"Never heard about it. I would say this was probably some fanfic you found on the internet, althought I gotta say, it's an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> My first thought when I saw the title was &quot;Wraiths from Antartica?&quot; Lol<br /> <br /> There's room from several other Dark Kingdoms to be made, that are conquered over the course of history. For example, while the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian is a good fit for the Meso-Americas, it's a poor fit for the North and South America.<br /> <br /> Here in South America, which is the region I can better describe because I live in it, the would be at the very least 4 or 5 Dark Kingdoms, just as an example, one for the andine deads (Chile and Peru), mostly aligned with the Incan Empire, another one for the natives of the north of South America (Colombia, Venezuela, Guyanas and north of Brazil), one for the central of Brazil, another for the Brazilian Sea Coast and one for the South of South America (Argentina and Uruguay). And that's by itself enormous already for each.<br /> <br /> In North America there would be similar divisions, in Europe besides the germanics/nordic regions, there would also be a &quot;proto-slavic&quot; Dark Kingdom to the east, another in Central Asia, probably a mongolian one in the far east, and all that before reaching China. I dont particularly agree with the Dark Kingdom of Jade &quot;colonizing&quot; Japan, Korea and Southeast Asia the way it does in WtO, much less in the way it does, even with the first emperor with his Terracota Army in the control. I think Southeast Asia would have at least one Dark Kingdom and the isolated Japan another.<br /> <br /> And Africa would also be similarly divided, I wouldnt even dare to try and do it thou, with so many large kingdoms that would be hard. Bantus, Yorubas, Malis, Kongoneses... The best would probably be to establish one DK to the East Coast, another to the West and a third to the South at the very least, for the Subsaaran regions, while north africa would've fallen to whatever DK existed under Carthago, only to be dominated by Stygia after the Punic wars, so North Africa would've been under the control of Stygia.<br /> <br /> That however could prove problematic after the islamic Caliphates took North Africa, unless Stygia decided to turn ALL new Wraiths in North Africa into fuel for the forges (like the DK of Jade do to the reast of Southeast Asia), but that would ignite and endless war with any number of Middle Eastern DK that could exist (althought constant war Between Stygia and Middle Eastern DK's may be inevitable either way ever since the 7th - 8th century with Islam).<br /> <br /> A DK of Ice would be interesting, and no doubt there would be conflicts with them and Stygia; I think that the Fishers would, funnily enough, be able to create comon ground and maybe even integration between the two however, with more and more fishers arising in both kingdoms. The same could hold true for the eastern slavic DK, especially once those 3 realized the potential of unity against the other DKs threats and against Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:57:10-07:00","id":1483915,"title":"","content":"Most of the pagan underworlds are best simulated by making them a Far Shore. That's pretty much by design. The actual afterlife is supposed to be BEYOND the Shadowlands and Dark Kingdoms. Those are just way stations before the Wraith reaches their &quot;final destination&quot; whether that is a Far Shore, Transcendence, Oblivion, or who knows what. There is probably both a Valhalla and Niflheim (perhaps multiple versions) among the Far Shores.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the writers at White Wolf forgot the plot when writing their new sourcebooks, and they frequently came up with duplicative ideas in their attempt to mine multiculturalism to get people to buy additional sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> I'd have no problem making Stygia the actual Dark Kingdom that still ferried the Norse wraiths to whatever Far Shore. It's just that the Ferrymen who did so would look more like Valkyries, Odins, and the other Norse Psychopomps than someone who looks like Charon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T22:27:38-07:00","id":1483957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1483797-dark-kingdom-of-ice?p=1483863#post1483863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 180 of Dark Ages Mage for specifics on Niflheim. Pages 174-181 for the whole section on the Dark Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1483797-dark-kingdom-of-ice?p=1483914#post1483914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, while the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian is a good fit for the Meso-Americas, it's a poor fit for the North and South America..</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats okay, \u200bthe original Dark Kingdoms of the Americas were the North American <b>Islands of Flint</b>, the Mesoamerican <b>Flayed Lands</b>, and the South American <b>Lands of Gold</b>.<br /> \u200bShame whats happened with them tho'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1483797-dark-kingdom-of-ice?p=1483914#post1483914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That however could prove problematic after the islamic Caliphates took North Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Mantaqat Khayal, the Shadowlands of the Middle East would have a few words in that matter too... ouch<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1483797-dark-kingdom-of-ice?p=1483915#post1483915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the pagan underworlds are best simulated by making them a Far Shore. That's pretty much by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, how true!<br /> <br /> Thank you for all of your replies and answers, helped a lot! &lt;3 <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}